    "Description": "The course provide students with solid background on the concepts and techniques of computer graphics: Raster Algorithms, Signal Processing, Viewing, Surface techniques, Ray Tracing, Texture Mapping, Data Structures for Graphics, Sampling, Curves, Computer Animation, Graphics Hardware, Light, Color, Visual Perception, Tone Reproduction, Global Illumination, Reflection Models, Image-Based Rendering, Visualization. One third of the contact time devoted for practicing on computer to master these techniques. This course give mathematical foundations of computer graphics with a focus on geometric intuition, allows the programmer to understand and apply those foundations to the development of efficient code.",
    "StudentTasks": "- Students must attend more than 80% of contact sessions in order to be accepted to the final examination. - Student is responsible to do all exercises given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time - Promptly access to the FU CMS at http://cms.fpt.edu.vn for up-to-date course information.",
    "Tools": "Tools: C++ for MFC (Microsoft Visual Studio), OpenGL, python (https://www.python.org), octave (http://www.gnu.org/software/octave/)",
